### Operational — never publish ###
# Deployment scripts hold the database password and the temporary logins;
# they live on the POS machine only.
scripts/*
# EXEMPT — the reason above does not reach these. They are not policy leaking; each is named
# here on its own merits, and anything new in scripts/ is still excluded by default.
#
# e2e-backend.sh is a TEST HARNESS, not a deployment script: it holds no credential beyond the
# local-dev defaults already committed in application.properties. docs/RUNBOOK.md and the e2e
# skill both point at it, so a clone without it has tests it cannot start.
#
# Written as `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so with `scripts/` the negation below would silently do nothing.
!scripts/e2e-backend.sh
# Runtime state written by the running app.
logs/
run/

# Vulnerability roadmaps. Stay local, even in a private repo: they name where the
# credentials and the unfixed weaknesses are, which is the one document you would not
# hand an attacker along with the source.
docs/security-audit-2026-09-03.md
docs/pre-internet-audit.md

### Build output ###
target/
!**/src/main/**/target/
!**/src/test/**/target/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
build/
!**/src/main/**/build/
!**/src/test/**/build/

